WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 4.3 · People, Culture & Volunteers
Contracts and terms

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Every working relationship needs written terms, starting with the one between co-founders.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
Every working relationship needs written terms that suit its type, starting with the one between co-founders. The document sets out the role, time, pay or expenses, ownership of work and how it ends.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Match the document to the relationship

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:40.833
Co-founders: A founders' agreement on roles, time, decisions, ownership of work and what happens if one leaves. For example: The two bakery founders agree who keeps the recipes if one of them leaves.

6
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:51.793
Employees: An employment contract or written statement that meets local minimum terms. For example: Each trainee signs a six-month contract with hours, pay, probation and a notice period.

7
00:00:51.793 --> 00:01:03.863
Contractors: A services agreement with deliverables and fees, for someone truly independent. For example: A web developer agrees to deliver the bakery's order page in six weeks for a set fee.

8
00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:16.763
Volunteers: A volunteer agreement or role description, without language of obligation or pay. For example: The retired baker at the stall gets a role description and claims travel expenses only.

9
00:01:17.163 --> 00:01:17.763
Why it matters

10
00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:23.807
1. Getting the type wrong from the start is a common legal risk.

11
00:01:23.807 --> 00:01:29.111
2. Clear ownership means what you create belongs to the organisation.

12
00:01:29.111 --> 00:01:35.044
3. A founders' agreement prevents painful disputes if someone leaves.

13
00:01:35.444 --> 00:01:36.044
What it guides

14
00:01:36.044 --> 00:01:40.607
1. Your onboarding: signed terms before the first day.

15
00:01:40.607 --> 00:01:45.911
2. Your people records: signed copies kept securely, renewal dates tracked.

16
00:01:45.911 --> 00:01:51.104
3. Your wider legal framework in Module 10.

17
00:01:51.504 --> 00:01:52.104
What to avoid

18
00:01:52.104 --> 00:01:58.148
Using a template without checking it with someone with a legal background.

19
00:01:58.148 --> 00:02:02.711
Volunteer agreements that accidentally create an employment relationship.

20
00:02:02.711 --> 00:02:07.904
Never updating terms when a role changes.

21
00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:10.304
You list each working relationship and the terms it needs.

22
00:02:10.304 --> 00:02:14.304
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:18.904
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
